architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-defect-scout.md:15:- `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:8` through `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:15` define a separate Pinia projection state with `elements2D`, `elements3D`, and `guides`, and `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:69` through `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:94` allow wholesale replacement/clearing of that projection. The file comment says this is not an authority at `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:17`, but the only live source consumer found in this scout is snapping.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-010-decision-conformance-refresh.md:11:- `frontend/src/App.vue:95` imports `useAppCanvasSession`, `frontend/src/App.vue:96` imports `useAppKeyboardShortcuts`, and `frontend/src/App.vue:98` imports `useDriveProjectSession`.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-010-decision-conformance-refresh.md:14:- `frontend/src/App.vue:216` delegates global keyboard behavior to `useAppKeyboardShortcuts(...)`.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-010-decision-conformance-refresh.md:25:- `frontend/src/composables/useAppKeyboardShortcuts.ts:24` exposes a composable that receives injected callbacks; it owns `keydown` handling and registers/unregisters the listener at `frontend/src/composables/useAppKeyboardShortcuts.ts:97` and `frontend/src/composables/useAppKeyboardShortcuts.ts:98`.
architecture-audit/final-review/00-summary.md:18:| ARCH-010 | resolved | App shell extraction in `frontend/src/App.vue:1`, `frontend/src/composables/useDriveProjectSession.ts:1`, `frontend/src/composables/useAppKeyboardShortcuts.ts:1`, `frontend/src/composables/useAppCanvasSession.ts:1`; log `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-010.md:1`. | None. |
architecture-audit/final-review/03-frontend-layering.md:7:`frontend/src/App.vue:1` is now a composition shell. Drive/project session behavior lives in `frontend/src/composables/useDriveProjectSession.ts:1`; keyboard routing lives in `frontend/src/composables/useAppKeyboardShortcuts.ts:1`; canvas/session read models live in `frontend/src/composables/useAppCanvasSession.ts:1`; reactive runtime snapshots are exposed by `frontend/src/composables/useProjectStateRuntimeSnapshot.ts:1`.
architecture-audit/final-review/08-persistence-drive.md:13:No migration reader, command stream replay path, private command-stack restore, old `elements2D`/`elements3D` DTO, or Drive last-file auto-open compatibility path remains. Legacy command/payload keys are rejected in `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:36`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:24`, and `frontend/tests/e2e/current-persistence-contract.spec.ts:67`.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:14:- The guards reject legacy command-stream and pre-current DTO fields (`commands`, `commandHistory`, `undoStack`, `redoStack`, `SerializedCommand`, `SerializedOperation`, `elements2D`, `elements3D`) at top-level and nested payload positions rather than accepting, migrating, or aliasing them.
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:19:| ARCH-010 | Resolved by selected Proposal A: extract App shell responsibilities into Drive/session/keyboard/canvas composables; see `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-010.md:1` and `architecture-audit/proposals/ARCH-010/proposal-a.md:1`. | Current extraction is visible in `frontend/src/App.vue:1`, `frontend/src/composables/useDriveProjectSession.ts:1`, `frontend/src/composables/useAppKeyboardShortcuts.ts:1`, and `frontend/src/composables/useAppCanvasSession.ts:1`; evidence is in `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-010.md:1` and `architecture-audit/final-review/03-frontend-layering.md:1`. | `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:1` now includes a focused static ARCH-010 guard requiring App.vue to compose through `useDriveProjectSession`, `useAppKeyboardShortcuts`, and `useAppCanvasSession`, rejecting reintroduced App-owned localStorage restoration, Drive singleton/private-access orchestration, inline autosave, keyboard listener, and canvas/session orchestration. The same guard checks the three composables own their intended current concerns without old localStorage compatibility, command/store keyboard authority, or Drive/persistence canvas coupling. | No unresolved App-shell risk. This optional hardening adds executable import/source-boundary checks while keeping ARCH-010 resolved. |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:60:Focused static App-shell boundary coverage was added in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:1` for the current shell in `frontend/src/App.vue:1`, Drive/session lifecycle in `frontend/src/composables/useDriveProjectSession.ts:1`, keyboard action router in `frontend/src/composables/useAppKeyboardShortcuts.ts:1`, and canvas/session boundary in `frontend/src/composables/useAppCanvasSession.ts:1`. The guard fails if App.vue reintroduces deleted `diedrico_last_file`/`localStorage` restoration, direct `new GoogleDriveService` orchestration, private Drive access, inline autosave timers/subscriptions, inline keydown listener orchestration, or canvas/session implementation details beyond handler wiring. It also asserts the Drive composable owns GoogleDriveService/ProjectService/autosave concerns without localStorage compatibility, the keyboard composable remains an injected-action router without command/store authority, and the canvas composable owns active-plane/coordinate/fit/cascade-preview concerns without Drive/project persistence coupling. ARCH-010 remains resolved by `architecture-audit/issues/register.md:1`; this is optional hardening only. Focused validation evidence is recorded in `.saivage/stages/ci-arch-010-app-shell-boundary-hardening/logs/focused-arch-010-guard-rerun.stdout.log:1`.
